    "linkedin:776624e0f3ad701d24fff181": {
      "job": {
        "title": "Full Stack Engineer (Typescript, Next)",
        "company": "Torentify",
        "location": "",
        "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482436401",
        "platform": "Linkedin",
        "date_posted": "",
        "is_remote": true,
        "description": "**About the Company** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Inclined is a well\\-funded startup developing technology that allows people to borrow against the value of their whole life insurance policies. The company is building systems to manage loan collateral, move funds securely, and automate processes that have traditionally relied on manual work. Its founding team includes experienced leaders from finance, software, and life insurance, including the co\\-founder of Strava and Guidewire.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**About the Role** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Inclined is looking for a Full\\-Stack Engineer to help develop its consumer lending product, underwriting and loan management systems, and internal tools for sales and operations teams. The role involves solving complex product challenges by turning varied loan requirements, eligibility rules, and business processes into clean, extensible code and straightforward user experiences.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n You'll work closely with engineering, product, design, and other stakeholders in a small, collaborative team. As part of Inclined's engineering culture, you'll also rotate through project leadership responsibilities, starting with smaller features and progressing to larger initiatives. This includes defining project scope, coordinating work, gathering domain knowledge, and communicating progress.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n The company operates as a distributed, remote\\-first team, using asynchronous communication and regular developer discussions to stay connected across time zones.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Key Responsibilities** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n* Build and maintain features across the consumer lending product, underwriting and loan systems, and internal business tools.\n* Translate complex loan requirements, eligibility rules, and edge cases into clean, maintainable, and extensible software.\n* Develop user experiences that make complex financial processes simple and reliable.\n* Own features and projects from initial concept through implementation and production launch.\n* Rotate through project leadership responsibilities, including defining scope, coordinating tasks, and monitoring and communicating progress.\n* Partner with product, design, and internal and external stakeholders to understand business requirements and plan effective solutions.\n* Contribute to initiatives involving underwriting automation, insurance carrier eligibility, mobile applications, and loan origination documents.\n* Collaborate with teammates through asynchronous communication and regular developer discussions.\n* Work independently across time zones while keeping colleagues informed and maintaining strong collaboration.\n* Use AI tools thoughtfully across development workflows, recognizing their limitations and involving people where appropriate.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Required Qualifications** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n* Approximately 4\\+ years of experience is a useful reference point, though demonstrated ownership and project experience matter more than a specific number of years.\n* A track record of shipping and owning production code, including taking features from concept through launch.\n* A generalist mindset and comfort working across the full stack.\n* Ability to develop simple, effective solutions to loosely defined problems.\n* Self\\-motivation and the ability to work through ambiguity in a remote environment.\n* Strong attention to detail and an appreciation for accuracy in complex workflows.\n* A collaborative, open\\-minded, flexible, and communicative approach.\n* A user\\-focused mindset and the ability to work effectively with colleagues across different functions.\n* Thoughtful use of AI tools, including an understanding of their limitations and the importance of human involvement.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Preferred Qualifications** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n* Experience in fintech or another regulated industry.\n* Experience working on products that move money.\n* Familiarity with Inclined's technology stack, including TypeScript, Next.js, React, GraphQL, Node.js, Prisma, AWS, Terraform, Docker, and dbt.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Location and Work Arrangement** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n* Fully remote within the United States.\n* Distributed, remote\\-first team with collaboration across time zones.\n* Asynchronous communication through Slack and regular synchronous developer discussions.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Compensation and Benefits** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n* Competitive salary and equity package.\n* Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, and life insurance benefits.\n* Generous vacation and holidays.\n* Remote\\-first working culture.\n* Opportunity to work with an experienced team.\n* Regular team offsites to connect in person, with previous trips to Truckee, Austin, and Minneapolis.",
        "job_id": "linkedin:776624e0f3ad701d24fff181",
