    "linkedin:a7b6e387708203c571d881ea": {
      "job": {
        "title": "Staff FrontEnd Engineer - Platform - App Core Usage | US | Remote",
        "company": "Ladders",
        "location": "",
        "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4480024652",
        "platform": "Linkedin",
        "date_posted": "",
        "is_remote": true,
        "description": "For our client, we are seeking a Staff FrontEnd Engineer \\- Platform \\- App Core Usage to join the team of a leader in the Technical Services space.\n   \n\n  \n\n This role will focus on building and evolving the core web experiences, backend services, and customer\\-facing workflows that support platform usage and billing\\-related operations. You will partner closely with cross\\-functional teams to deliver reliable, scalable features that improve the customer experience while strengthening internal systems and processes. The position also calls for technical leadership in a remote\\-first environment, with an emphasis on mentorship, execution, and continuous improvement across distributed systems.\n   \n\n  \n\n Location: Remote \\- US based candidates only, no visa sponsorship available\n   \n\n  \n\n Compensation: $174,986 – $209,983 annually\n   \n\n  \n\n**Responsibilities**\n* Design and develop full\\-stack web applications and customer portals\n* Build and maintain backend APIs and user interfaces using modern technologies\n* Integrate systems with external platforms like NetSuite and Salesforce\n* Automate business logic for usage metering and billing processes\n* Collaborate with cross\\-functional teams to deliver comprehensive features\n* Optimize CI/CD pipelines and enhance system observability\n* Provide technical leadership and mentorship to team members\n\n\n**Qualifications**\n* 1\\+ years of fully remote work experience\n* Experience with large SaaS platforms and distributed systems challenges\n* Strong backend skills in Golang and Node.js\n* Proficient in frontend technologies like TypeScript and React\n* Demonstrated ability to deliver projects independently from concept to deployment\n* Experience mentoring junior engineers in a remote setting\n* Strong Kubernetes knowledge in cloud environments (AWS, GCP, Azure)\n* Familiarity with infrastructure\\-as\\-code tools (Helm, Terraform, Jsonnet)\n\n\n**Benefits**\n* Remote\\-first work environment\n* Opportunity to contribute to open source projects\n* Collaborative culture across diverse teams\n* Ownership through Restricted Stock Units (RSUs)\n* Focus on professional development and mentorship opportunities\n\n\n Our client is an equal opportunity employer. We encourage you to apply even if you don’t meet every qualification—your background could be exactly what this team needs.",
